    *a payment* received by individual; scenario element.
    *a payment* is program established prior to july first nineteen seventy three; scenario element.
    *a payment* is program established prior to july first nineteen seventy three and subsequently amended to conform to state or federal constitutional standards; scenario element.
    the payment made by state of which receiving individual of *a payment* is resident; scenario element.
    *a payment* is payment program eligibility not based on need; scenario element.
    *a payment* is payment program eligibility based solely on required age and state residency; scenario element.
    *a payment* is individual first became eligible individual or eligible spouse on or before september thirtieth nineteen eighty five; scenario element.
    the individual residency years under program as in effect prior to january first nineteen eighty three of *a payment* is *a number*; scenario element.

the knowledge base us_statutes_42_1382a_b_2 includes:


% 42 U.S.C. 1382a(b)(2) — us:statutes/42/1382a/b/2
the text of "42 USC 1382a(b)(2)(A)" is at "sources/us/statutes/42/1382a/b/2.yaml".

the text of "42 USC 1382a(b)(2)(B)(ii)" is at "sources/us/statutes/42/1382a/b/2.yaml".

the text of "42 USC 1382a(b)(2)(B)(iii)(II)" is at "sources/us/statutes/42/1382a/b/2.yaml".

the text of "42 USC 1382a(b)(2)(B)" is at "sources/us/statutes/42/1382a/b/2.yaml".

the annual general income exclusion limit is 240, as stated in "42 USC 1382a(b)(2)(A)".

the default state age payment age is 65, as stated in "42 USC 1382a(b)(2)(B)(ii)".

the state age payment residency year requirement is 25, as stated in "42 USC 1382a(b)(2)(B)(iii)(II)".

rule annual_general_income_excluded with provenance "42 USC 1382a(b)(2)(A)":
the annual general income excluded of a person is an amount N if
    the annual income not paid on basis of need of the person is an amount M
    and the annual general income exclusion limit is an amount K
    and the maximum of 0 and M is a number P
    and the minimum of P and K is N.

rule state_age_residency_payment_excluded_1 with provenance "42 USC 1382a(b)(2)(B)":
a payment is state age residency payment excluded if
    the payment is monthly or other periodic
    and the payment received by individual
    and the payment is program established prior to july first nineteen seventy three
    and the payment made by state of which receiving individual of the payment is resident
    and the payment is payment program eligibility not based on need
    and the payment is payment program eligibility based solely on required age and state residency
    and the payment is individual first became eligible individual or eligible spouse on or before september thirtieth nineteen eighty five
    and the individual residency years under program as in effect prior to january first nineteen eighty three of the payment is a number N
    and the state age payment residency year requirement is a number M
    and N >= M.

rule state_age_residency_payment_excluded_2 with provenance "42 USC 1382a(b)(2)(B)":
a payment is state age residency payment excluded if
    the payment is monthly or other periodic
    and the payment received by individual
    and the payment is program established prior to july first nineteen seventy three and subsequently amended to conform to state or federal constitutional standards
    and the payment made by state of which receiving individual of the payment is resident
    and the payment is payment program eligibility not based on need
    and the payment is payment program eligibility based solely on required age and state residency
    and the payment is individual first became eligible individual or eligible spouse on or before september thirtieth nineteen eighty five
    and the individual residency years under program as in effect prior to january first nineteen eighty three of the payment is a number N
    and the state age payment residency year requirement is a number M
    and N >= M.

scenario annual_general_income_exclusion_capped_at_240 is, as stated in "sources/us/statutes/42/1382a/b/2.test.yaml" at case 1:
    person_1 is a person.
    the annual income not paid on basis of need of person_1 is 300.
    q_annual_general_income_excluded expects answers ["the annual general income excluded of person_1 is 240"].

